content:
maria: OnyxRetail onboarding hit a reproducible 429 pattern during their demo. Mobile app cold-start spawns preflight + token mint from the app and a background sync worker; both run immediately on login. Happens ~12s after login.

maria: excerpt from their demo logs:
```
[2026-05-10T14:22:11Z] app-main init /v1/preflight 200
[2026-05-10T14:22:12Z] bg-sync mint /v1/token 429 x 10
[2026-05-10T14:22:12Z] webview init /v1/preflight 429 x 8
[2026-05-10T14:22:13Z] app-main retry /v1/preflight 429
```

devon: Which SDK version and how are they doing auth? Shared key in the app or short-lived session tokens?

maria: React Native SDK v1.7.9. They embedded a dev server key into the APK for the demo to avoid backend plumbing.

yuki: That explains it 44a shared key across processes + no splay = burst. Two routes affected: /v1/preflight and /v1/token. Recommend immediate customer-side mitigations and a fast ops smoothing while they rework auth.

yuki: Customer-side quick fixes to suggest now: 1) defer non-critical init until app focus or first interaction, 2) add a small randomized init jitter per process, 3) use a single mint-per-user-per-device pattern via local storage lock so background workers reuse the token. Example snippets: 

// RN init jitter + inflight guard
const jitter = () => 200 + Math.floor(Math.random()*900); // 200-1100ms
if (global.__RI_init) return;
setTimeout(()=>{ if (global.__RI_init) return; global.__RI_init = true; sdk.init().finally(()=> global.__RI_init = false); }, jitter());

// simple local lock for minting
const LOCK_KEY = 'onyx_mint_lock';
if (AsyncStorage.getItem(LOCK_KEY)) {
  // another process is minting, poll/backoff
} else {
  AsyncStorage.setItem(LOCK_KEY, '1');
  try { await fetch('/internal/mint'); } finally { AsyncStorage.removeItem(LOCK_KEY); }
}

maria: Great. Can ops apply a transient server-side change to buy time?

yuki: Ops options: enable tenant preflight_coalesce for "onyxretail", enable token_mint_coalesce, and temporarily increase the burst window by +170 tokens with TTL=45m. Also recommend adding a 2s leaky-bucket smoothing on both routes for that tenant.

ops-bot: RateLimitAlert: tenant="onyxretail" detected 429 surge 2026-05-10T14:22:10Z..2026-05-10T14:25:00Z peak_preflight=162 req/min peak_mint=88 req/min. Suggested: preflight_coalesce=true, token_mint_coalesce=true, burst_window_inc=+170, leaky_window=2000ms, ttl=45m.

devon: I'll open an infra change request with those flags and TTL. Maria, can you confirm OnyxEng can flip to ephemeral tokens this afternoon?

maria: Yes, they confirmed a 1-hour maintenance window starting in ~2 hours. They'll ship a quick backend endpoint to mint 60s tokens and add the AsyncStorage lock.

yuki: Post-change checks: monitor 429s for 2 hours, capture 10 init traces and 5 mint traces, confirm token header changes per-device, and watch preflight latency. If 429s persist after client splay + ephemeral tokens + coalesce, escalate to runtime team for more granular batching and KV-cache tuning.

maria: I'll send the client snippets + a sample mint proxy to the customer and schedule the maintenance. Updating the onboarding ticket and looping the solutions engineer. Thanks :pray:
